[[Open This|1. Create silo and upload TLS certificate]]

---

The first step of silo setup is creating the silo record and importing a matching TLS certificate. Virtual resource quotas are required during silo creation, and can be modified afterwards.

See the Resource Management guide for additional information regarding capacity planning and managing quotas.

The following information is required when creating a silo:

|attribute|value|h
|`name`|Must start with a letter and contain only lower-case letters, numbers, and dashes.|
|`description`|A brief description of the silo context and purpose.|
|`discoverable`|Whether the silo should be included in silo listing queries (non-discoverable silos are accessible only by direct name or id reference).|
|`identity_mode`|There are three identity modes, saml_jit, saml_scim, and local_only. See Authentication Configuration below for details on each.|
|`admin_group_name`|Required if using saml_jit or saml_scim identity modes; specifies which IdP group will be granted the Silo Admin role. The group is created in Oxide upon the first successful SAML login that includes this group attribute value.|
|`mapped_fleet_roles`|Optional mappings of fleet-level roles conferred by silo roles, applicable to the saml_jit and saml_scim modes only.|
|`quotas`|<$transclude tiddler="meh006" mode="block"/>|
|`tls_certificates`|<$transclude tiddler="meh007" mode="block"/>|
	
